{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ஈ","gloss":"give"},{"text":"தல்","lemma":"தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"giving"},{"surface":"எளிதே","parts":[{"text":"எளிது","lemma":"எளிது","gloss":"easy"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is easy indeed"},{"surface":"மாவண்","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"மா","gloss":"great"},{"text":"வண்","lemma":"வண்மை","gloss":"generosity"}],"gloss":"greatly generous"},{"surface":"தோன்றல்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்றல்","lemma":"தோன்றல்","gloss":"lord/noble"}],"gloss":"lord"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அது","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"நற்கு","parts":[{"text":"நற்கு","lemma":"நற்கு","gloss":"well"}],"gloss":"well","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அறிந்தனை","parts":[{"text":"அறிந்தனை","lemma":"அறிந்தனை","gloss":"you know"}],"gloss":"you know","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யாயின்","parts":[{"text":"யாயின்","lemma":"யாயின்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொது","parts":[{"text":"பொது","lemma":"பொது","gloss":"common/equal"}],"gloss":"common"},{"surface":"நோக்கு","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கு","lemma":"நோக்கு","gloss":"gaze/look"}],"gloss":"gaze"},{"surface":"ஒழிமதி","parts":[{"text":"ஒழி","lemma":"ஒழி","gloss":"abandon"},{"text":"மதி","lemma":"மதி","gloss":"honorific imperative suffix"}],"gloss":"please abandon"},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"புலவர்","gloss":"poets"}],"gloss":"poets"},{"surface":"மாட்டே","parts":[{"text":"மாட்டு","lemma":"மாட்டு","gloss":"towards"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"towards"}]}],"literal":"Thinking of one man in one direction, from the four directions / many people will come, seekers of gifts. / Knowing their worth is difficult indeed, greatly; / giving is easy indeed, O greatly generous lord! / If you know that well, / please abandon looking equally towards poets.","translation":"Thinking of just one man in one direction, seekers of gifts come from all four directions. O greatly generous lord, giving is very easy, but evaluating their true worth is extremely difficult. If you understand this well, please abandon looking at all poets with the same common gaze.","modern":"ஒரு திசையில் உள்ள ஒருவனை நினைத்து, நான்கு திசைகளிலிருந்தும் பரிசில் பெறும் மக்கள் பலர் வருவார்கள். சிறந்த கொடையாளியான தலைவனே! அவர்களுக்குக் கொடுப்பது மிகவும் எளிது; ஆனால் அவர்களின் தகுதியை அறிந்து கொடுப்பது மிகவும் அரிது. அதனை நீ நன்றாக உணர்ந்திருப்பின், புலவர்களிடம் காட்டும் பொதுவான பார்வையை ஒழிப்பாயாக.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Kapilar addresses the generous patron Malaiyamāṉ Tirumuṭikkāri. He points out that because of the king's fame, many seekers of gifts travel from all directions to see him. Kapilar advises the king that while giving away wealth is easy for a generous ruler, discerning the true merit and poetic caliber of each visitor is extremely difficult. He urges the king not to look at all poets with a uniform, common gaze (பொது நோக்கு), but to recognize and reward each according to their individual worth (வரிசை). This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Poruṇmoḻik kāñci tuṟai, as it offers wise counsel on virtue and discernment.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,2.0],[2.0,2.5],[2.5,2.8],[2.8,3.0],[3.0,3.4],[3.4,4.6],[4.6,5.1],[5.1,5.2],[5.2,5.9],[5.9,6.7],[6.7,6.7],[6.7,7.1],[7.1,7.6],[7.6,8.7],[8.7,9.1],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,9.6],[9.6,10.12],[10.12,10.9],[10.9,11.4],[11.4,11.8],[11.8,12.0]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,2.1],[2.1,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.5],[3.5,3.8],[3.8,5.1],[5.1,5.6],[5.6,5.7],[5.7,6.5],[6.5,7.4],[7.4,7.8],[7.8,7.9],[7.9,8.4],[8.4,9.5],[9.5,9.9],[9.9,10.4],[10.42,10.5],[10.5,10.98],[10.98,11.7],[11.7,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,12.9]]}}